      "blocks": {
        "l1": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Water deeper than the sock",
            "body": "<p>A sock is open at the top. Step into water higher than the cuff and it fills, the same as any sock. The only thing that changes where that line sits is how tall the sock is.</p>",
            "width": "1",
            "tone": "wash"
          }
        },
        "l2": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Very hard work, for a long time",
            "body": "<p>Breathability is real and it has a limit. Work hard enough for long enough and your foot produces vapour faster than the layer can move it. You end up damp from the inside instead of the outside.</p>",
            "width": "1",
            "tone": "wash"
          }
        },
        "l3": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A hole in the waterproof layer",
            "body": "<p>Once it’s pierced — by a toenail, a thorn, a sharp stone inside a boot — the waterproofing is gone and can’t be put back. No wash, spray or reproofing treatment brings it back.</p>",
            "width": "2",
            "tone": "blue"
          }
        }
      },
